      "question": "2. What is the next action, who is it for, and through which channel?",
      "answer": "(a) Ask the landlord to approve or reject the £79.35 + VAT overrun, via the approval request APR-103 (internal channel; no landlord contact on file, so it needs routing). (b) Email Clarke, contractor, on the existing thread (event 031): ask for photos of the completed work and a breakdown of the increase. Both are done and verified (A5, A6). Payment hold HOLD-102 (A3) stays in place."
    },
    {
      "question": "3. Does anything need a human decision, and why?",
      "answer": "Yes. Approving spend above the approved quote is the landlord's decision, not the agency's. The landlord must approve or reject the £79.35 + VAT overrun. Until then no payment should be released. Nothing else needs escalation at this stage."
    }
  ],
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "description": "Recorded contractor quote Q-101: £198.37 + VAT (£238.04 inc VAT), source event 008 and landlord approval event 011."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Recorded invoice 2311 for £333.26 inc VAT, payable by landlord direct."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "description": "Placed payment hold HOLD-102 on Clarke's invoice pending landlord approval of the overrun."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A4",
      "description": "Recorded work result as completed, based on the contractor's email; photos not yet received."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A5",
      "description": "Requested landlord approval APR-103 for the £79.35 + VAT overrun."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A6",
      "description": "Emailed contractor Clarke (MSG-104) asking for photos and a breakdown of the increase."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A7",
      "description": "Put the ticket on hold, waiting for the landlord, with review on 2025-10-15."
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [],
  "conflicts": [
    "The invoice check (A2) returned 'Invoice matches the approval', but £333.26 inc VAT (£277.72 + VAT) does not match the approved £198.37 + VAT (£238.04 inc VAT). I trusted the arithmetic and the source email, so the hold was placed.",
    "The contractor email (event 025) refers to 'the studio', but the job is for Flat 8 lounge. The contractor's 'all done at the studio' wording may be a template error. Confirm with photos.",
    "The check-out report is dated 25 August 2026, but the case is in October 2025. Treated as a record date error; no effect on the repair scope.",
    "The property is shown as NOT TENANTED (event 015), so the ticket was moved to Paused. The ticket record shows stage 'result' and a waiting-for-provider hold. Treated as a void property with the landlord paying."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The landlord who approved the quote (event 011) is the landlord to approve the overrun. No landlord contact is on the property record, so routing is internal.",
    "The property is void, so the landlord pays for the repair and no tenant deposit deduction arises at this stage.",
    "The contractor's completion statement is taken as provisional until photos are received."
  ]
}

